WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.099 --> 00:00:04.350
It's like when Luke Skywalker's dad died,
so Luke Skywalker wound up having to kill

00:00:04.350 --> 00:00:05.520
all those child Jedi.

00:00:05.520 --> 00:00:09.610
Yes, that's exactly what ... Wait, is that
what happened?

00:00:09.610 --> 00:00:12.140
I mean, a little.

00:00:14.030 --> 00:00:17.750
Tom, which Marvel characters do you think
will not survive phase four?

00:00:17.750 --> 00:00:19.890
What a bleak prospect.

00:00:19.890 --> 00:00:21.380
This is dark.

00:00:21.380 --> 00:00:22.380
That's what we do.

00:00:22.380 --> 00:00:24.869
That's what we do here.

00:00:24.869 --> 00:00:29.610
So I feel like there are two obvious answers
here, and they're both Ant-Man, right?

00:00:29.610 --> 00:00:32.960
I feel like Hank Pym can't last much longer,
right?

00:00:32.960 --> 00:00:33.960
No.

00:00:33.960 --> 00:00:36.170
Hank Pym was on my shortlist.

00:00:36.170 --> 00:00:37.569
He's the-

00:00:37.569 --> 00:00:38.770
Pun intended.

00:00:38.770 --> 00:00:40.710
Oh, Brian.

00:00:40.710 --> 00:00:42.649
Thank you.

00:00:42.649 --> 00:00:44.300
Bringing the fire.

00:00:44.300 --> 00:00:46.280
I'm feeling a little punchy.

00:00:46.280 --> 00:00:47.280
Feeling good.

00:00:47.280 --> 00:00:48.679
A little punchy?

00:00:48.679 --> 00:00:51.379
A little punchy.

00:00:51.379 --> 00:00:52.870
This is a terrific show we've made.

00:00:52.870 --> 00:00:53.870
Oh, wow.

00:00:53.870 --> 00:00:54.870
He's just riffing now.

00:00:54.870 --> 00:00:55.870
Go on.

00:00:55.870 --> 00:00:56.870
Hank Pym.

00:00:56.870 --> 00:00:57.870
Go on.

00:00:57.870 --> 00:00:58.870
Hank Pym.

00:00:58.870 --> 00:00:59.870
Hank Pym.

00:00:59.870 --> 00:01:00.870
Tell us about Hank Pym.

00:01:00.870 --> 00:01:03.549
I feel like he's gone from kind of jerk to
father figure a little bit over the last few

00:01:03.549 --> 00:01:04.549
movies.

00:01:04.549 --> 00:01:09.810
I don't feel like older father figures necessarily
do too well in hero's journeys.

00:01:09.810 --> 00:01:10.810
Yeah.

00:01:10.810 --> 00:01:15.119
I can't imagine that Hank Pym's going to last
too long.

00:01:15.119 --> 00:01:17.740
There's also Scott Lang, who's terrific.

00:01:17.740 --> 00:01:22.620
We all love Scott Lang, but he does fit into
a lot of the categories that I think previously

00:01:22.620 --> 00:01:27.110
murdered superheroes in the MCU fall into.

00:01:27.110 --> 00:01:32.930
Mostly, he's got a younger girl version of
him to take over for him right out the bat.

00:01:32.930 --> 00:01:37.780
Like, Quicksilver had Scarlet Witch ready
to step in as soon as he died.

00:01:37.780 --> 00:01:42.159
And Black Widow died, and then it turned out
that there was another Florence Pugh Black

00:01:42.159 --> 00:01:44.090
Widow.

00:01:44.090 --> 00:01:46.939
Scott Lang, he's got his daughter, Cassie.

00:01:46.939 --> 00:01:48.120
She's ready to step in.

00:01:48.120 --> 00:01:51.619
If you read the comics, they did murder her
pretty good.

00:01:51.619 --> 00:01:52.619
Yikes.

00:01:52.619 --> 00:01:59.999
But, I feel like they've been setting up for
her to fill the big shoes or small shoes,

00:01:59.999 --> 00:02:00.999
depending.

00:02:00.999 --> 00:02:03.799
Well, they do get big because she grows.

00:02:03.799 --> 00:02:08.020
Her superhero name is Stature.

00:02:08.020 --> 00:02:12.980
Cassie Lang, in the comics, is one of the
Young Avengers along with Isaiah Bradley's

00:02:12.980 --> 00:02:19.080
grandson, who we've seen Falcon and the Winter
Soldier, along with the other Hawkeye who

00:02:19.080 --> 00:02:23.550
we'll see in Hawkeye TV show, played by Hailee
Steinfeld.

00:02:23.550 --> 00:02:24.720
Kate Bishop.

00:02:24.720 --> 00:02:27.960
Wanda Maximoff's two kids, Billy and ... Billy?

00:02:27.960 --> 00:02:29.810
What was the other one's name?

00:02:29.810 --> 00:02:30.810
Tommy.

00:02:30.810 --> 00:02:31.810
Tommy.

00:02:31.810 --> 00:02:32.810
Tommy.

00:02:32.810 --> 00:02:33.810
I think Billy and Willie would have been better.

00:02:33.810 --> 00:02:34.810
I don't know where you got that.

00:02:34.810 --> 00:02:35.810
No?

00:02:35.810 --> 00:02:36.810
No.

00:02:36.810 --> 00:02:37.810
Terrific pitch.

00:02:37.810 --> 00:02:41.370
So, they were Speed and Wiccan.

00:02:41.370 --> 00:02:50.080
And then there was ... Kang had a past self
that came to the past, from the future, as

00:02:50.080 --> 00:02:53.040
a kid, as a hero named Iron Lad.

00:02:53.040 --> 00:02:57.000
So now, we've got Kang as well, and multiple
versions of Kang running around.

00:02:57.000 --> 00:03:01.080
And then, we've got Hulkling, who was a Skrull,
so we've got Skrulls.

00:03:01.080 --> 00:03:05.810
So all the pieces are in the places that we
need for a Young Avengers team to happen.

00:03:05.810 --> 00:03:09.390
I mean, how are they not going to dip into
the Young Avengers well, at some point?

00:03:09.390 --> 00:03:11.850
They've got to.

00:03:11.850 --> 00:03:12.850
Yeah.

00:03:12.850 --> 00:03:16.810
I think they're pretty clearly setting that
up, and then, in addition, I think what you're

00:03:16.810 --> 00:03:21.200
suggesting, Tom, if you kill off Scott Lang,
that's a pretty good motivator for someone

00:03:21.200 --> 00:03:26.180
to be like, "Well, I'll take over for my dad
and do what he couldn't."

00:03:26.180 --> 00:03:32.660
Or, same deal, even if Hank Pym were to go,
you could have a similar kind of inspiring,

00:03:32.660 --> 00:03:37.570
"Now that now that Papa Pym has gone, I'll
be the new Papa Pym."

00:03:37.570 --> 00:03:38.570
Right.

00:03:38.570 --> 00:03:39.670
"But a lady Papa Pym."

00:03:39.670 --> 00:03:44.230
It's like when Luke Skywalker's dad died,
so Luke Skywalker wound up having to kill

00:03:44.230 --> 00:03:45.580
all those child Jedi.

00:03:45.580 --> 00:03:49.980
Yes, that's exactly what ... Wait, is that
what happened?

00:03:49.980 --> 00:03:51.570
I mean, a little.

00:03:51.570 --> 00:03:52.570
Maybe a little.

00:03:52.570 --> 00:03:53.620
He thought about it, just for a second.

00:03:53.620 --> 00:03:54.620
He thought about it, yeah.

00:03:54.620 --> 00:03:55.770
That's a pretty good pick, yeah.

00:03:55.770 --> 00:03:57.660
We were watching different Rise of Skywalkers?

00:03:57.660 --> 00:03:58.890
Yeah, all right.

00:03:58.890 --> 00:03:59.890
Yeah.

00:03:59.890 --> 00:04:00.890
That was a good pick.

00:04:00.890 --> 00:04:05.160
I think that Scott Lang or Hank Pym ... I
think Hank Pym is a lot more likely than Scott

00:04:05.160 --> 00:04:06.160
Lang.

00:04:06.160 --> 00:04:07.160
Got to be, right?

00:04:07.160 --> 00:04:08.160
It's a bummer.

00:04:08.160 --> 00:04:12.040
Just because Michael Douglas, he's an older
guy, and I don't think he's going to want

00:04:12.040 --> 00:04:13.220
to do Marvel movies forever.

00:04:13.220 --> 00:04:16.390
Yeah, he wants to go hang out with Catherine
Zeta-Jones and live his life.

00:04:16.390 --> 00:04:18.350
And for that, I respect him.

00:04:18.350 --> 00:04:20.180
I also want to do that.

00:04:20.180 --> 00:04:24.130
It's a lot of time to walk around with little
dots painted on his face so they can make it look

00:04:24.130 --> 00:04:25.300
like Wall Street again.

00:04:25.300 --> 00:04:26.300
Yeah.

00:04:26.300 --> 00:04:31.040
I mean, with the return of the original Wasp,
with Michelle Pfeiffer showing up at the end

00:04:31.040 --> 00:04:35.610
of Ant-Man and the Wasp, now we've got that
character in there.

00:04:35.610 --> 00:04:42.600
And, again, from a storytelling perspective,
if you have both of these elder, older heroes

00:04:42.600 --> 00:04:46.170
running around, it makes sense for one of
them to go, again, to provide motivation to

00:04:46.170 --> 00:04:49.570
the younger heroes to go do heroic things.

00:04:49.570 --> 00:04:53.110
The balance needs to be imbalanced in a way,
you know what I mean?

00:04:53.110 --> 00:04:55.980
So I think that it makes some sense for that
to happen.

00:04:55.980 --> 00:04:57.010
So, that's a good pick.

00:04:57.010 --> 00:05:00.440
Yeah, you get the wrap up a redemptive arc
for Hank.

00:05:00.440 --> 00:05:04.900
He gets to stop being a jerk and do the whole,
"Ah, I'm sorry for everything I did, everything

00:05:04.900 --> 00:05:05.900
wrong."

00:05:05.900 --> 00:05:09.420
Well, and even though Hank's more likely,
Scott could also have that too, right?

00:05:09.420 --> 00:05:13.960
He could come full circle as a dad and as
a human, and that could be ... Because Marvel

00:05:13.960 --> 00:05:19.280
does like to cut the actor off when their
whole story arc is complete because then,

00:05:19.280 --> 00:05:21.230
they're like, "Well, what do we do with you
now?"

00:05:21.230 --> 00:05:25.010
Yeah, and we don't want Paul Rudd to be collecting
too many paychecks over this time.

00:05:25.010 --> 00:05:26.010
He's been in a lot of movies.

00:05:26.010 --> 00:05:29.750
I personally want him to get all the paychecks
that he wants and deserves.

00:05:29.750 --> 00:05:33.940
He needs to find a new talk show to show that
Mack and Me footage on.

00:05:33.940 --> 00:05:38.050
He just needs to show up on Conan's HBO show
and just show it for no reason.

00:05:38.050 --> 00:05:39.580
There you go.

00:05:39.580 --> 00:05:40.930
they'll just recreate it.

00:05:40.930 --> 00:05:41.930
Yeah.

00:05:41.930 --> 00:05:42.930
Makes sense to me.

00:05:42.930 --> 00:05:44.400
Nina, what's your pick?

00:05:44.400 --> 00:05:50.740
So, it's funny, I kind of went with the similar
idea to someone can take over.

00:05:50.740 --> 00:05:54.490
No one is going to be surprised that I picked
Hawkeye because I don't like him.

00:05:54.490 --> 00:05:56.540
I don't want to watch him anymore.

00:05:56.540 --> 00:06:00.300
But I'm also like, Kate Bishop's right there.

00:06:00.300 --> 00:06:02.220
He's going to have this TV show.

00:06:02.220 --> 00:06:06.450
How much mileage can we really get out of
this guy? Jeremy Renner has music to make.

00:06:06.450 --> 00:06:08.230
Things got to happen.

00:06:08.230 --> 00:06:10.160
He's got to bring the app back.

00:06:10.160 --> 00:06:11.720
Yeah, he's got to relaunch his app.

00:06:11.720 --> 00:06:16.390
But yeah, I don't think Hawkeye's in this
for the long haul.

00:06:16.390 --> 00:06:20.510
If they're setting him up with a Young Avenger,
and that was kind of my exact same thinking

00:06:20.510 --> 00:06:25.000
is like, Kate Bishop will want to avenge him
in the same way that Yelena wants to avenge

00:06:25.000 --> 00:06:26.000
her sister.

00:06:26.000 --> 00:06:33.770
If Yelena kills him, that would be kind of
cool.

00:06:33.770 --> 00:06:37.850
But also, he's getting a whole series of his
name on it, so it's probably not going to

00:06:37.850 --> 00:06:38.850
happen.

00:06:38.850 --> 00:06:43.710
Yeah, it seems unlikely, but the fact that
they are adding a second character who goes

00:06:43.710 --> 00:06:46.080
by Hawkeye to the show called Hawkeye.

00:06:46.080 --> 00:06:47.770
That's what I'm saying.

00:06:47.770 --> 00:06:54.960
And the second Hawkeye is played by Academy
Award nominee, Hailee Steinfeld.

00:06:54.960 --> 00:07:01.540
Well isn't the first Hawkeye played by Academy
Award nominee, Jeremy Renner?

00:07:01.540 --> 00:07:03.960
She's younger, so it's more impressive.

00:07:03.960 --> 00:07:06.650
I'm just saying, if you're going to bring
in the bonafides, you got to be-

00:07:06.650 --> 00:07:10.860
No, I think what I'm saying is they didn't
bring in some like newcomer.

00:07:10.860 --> 00:07:13.919
They brought in someone very, very famous.

00:07:13.919 --> 00:07:14.919
Sure.

00:07:14.919 --> 00:07:15.919
That's true.

00:07:15.919 --> 00:07:18.550
I thought you were saying, "Hailee Steinfeld
was just straight up a more legit actor."

00:07:18.550 --> 00:07:24.510
Well ... No, I'm not saying.

00:07:24.510 --> 00:07:31.210
There's also the cynical, logical part of
me that feels like, aside from Hawkeye, it'll

00:07:31.210 --> 00:07:35.669
be Julia Louis-Dreyfus' Contessa because how
long does that woman really want to stay in

00:07:35.669 --> 00:07:36.669
the MCU?

00:07:36.669 --> 00:07:37.669
Well, yeah.

00:07:37.669 --> 00:07:38.669
I mean, I think that she's-

00:07:38.669 --> 00:07:39.850
How long are the checks going to clear?

00:07:39.850 --> 00:07:41.740
Yeah, she's set up for a while, I think.

00:07:41.740 --> 00:07:42.740
She's kind of the-

00:07:42.740 --> 00:07:47.540
She is, but it's also, if that woman, with
all of her armloads of Emmys, was like, "I

00:07:47.540 --> 00:07:49.199
don't want to do this anymore."

00:07:49.199 --> 00:07:53.540
She could get herself written off in dramatic
fashion if need be.

00:07:53.540 --> 00:07:56.740
I mean, she's clearly being set up to be available.

00:07:56.740 --> 00:08:00.300
She's clearly being set up to be kind of the
anti-Nick Fury.

00:08:00.300 --> 00:08:01.949
Will she go at the end of phase four?

00:08:01.949 --> 00:08:03.800
Phase four is a long one.

00:08:03.800 --> 00:08:10.050
It's a few years, so it's possible that at
the end of this phase, at whatever big showdown

00:08:10.050 --> 00:08:15.730
her character is building these anti-Avengers
for, maybe she'll bite the dust.

00:08:15.730 --> 00:08:19.050
I think she'll last a little bit longer.

00:08:19.050 --> 00:08:20.050
She's kind of in the background.

00:08:20.050 --> 00:08:22.730
You think she'll move into a subsequent phase?

00:08:22.730 --> 00:08:25.850
I think that she could because, again, what
is she being asked to do?

00:08:25.850 --> 00:08:27.870
She's not getting strapped to any rigs, right?

00:08:27.870 --> 00:08:29.540
She doesn't have to fly around.

00:08:29.540 --> 00:08:32.889
She doesn't have to sit through and get like
a bunch of makeup slathered on her face.

00:08:32.889 --> 00:08:38.139
She puts on cool sunglasses and a purple streak
in her hair, and she just makes jokes, and

00:08:38.139 --> 00:08:39.139
that's it.

00:08:39.139 --> 00:08:43.550
She's basically just doing sitcom stuff and
making Marvel money.

00:08:43.550 --> 00:08:47.569
That's a fair point, but I also am just like,
if I were Julia Louis-Dreyfus, I think I'd

00:08:47.569 --> 00:08:51.170
be like, "I want to do a couple of these max."

00:08:51.170 --> 00:08:52.170
That's fair.

00:08:52.170 --> 00:08:54.569
But, I could be wrong, and I don't want her
to get killed off.

00:08:54.569 --> 00:08:58.110
I am thrilled anytime I see Julia Louis-Dreyfus
do literally anything.

00:08:58.110 --> 00:09:02.260
I would watch a movie of her just sitting
in a chair for six hours because it would

00:09:02.260 --> 00:09:03.300
probably be really funny.

00:09:03.300 --> 00:09:04.300
We might get it.

00:09:04.300 --> 00:09:05.300
Yeah.

00:09:05.300 --> 00:09:06.949
But yeah, I'd enjoy it.

00:09:06.949 --> 00:09:12.379
But no, I don't want her to get killed off,
but I'm very cynical about how actors make

00:09:12.379 --> 00:09:14.649
decisions about their lives and their livelihoods.

00:09:14.649 --> 00:09:17.830
And also, she has Seinfeld money.

00:09:17.830 --> 00:09:19.769
This is not about checks for this woman.

00:09:19.769 --> 00:09:21.480
Yeah, that's true.

00:09:21.480 --> 00:09:22.480
She can write her own TV.

00:09:22.480 --> 00:09:23.480
She can do whatever.

00:09:23.480 --> 00:09:24.490
Yeah, she's fine.

00:09:24.490 --> 00:09:25.800
Yeah.

00:09:25.800 --> 00:09:28.529
She's not hurting.

00:09:28.529 --> 00:09:31.080
I had a list of names that I came up with.

00:09:31.080 --> 00:09:36.100
I had a few, and I have one ultimate pick,
but I'm just going to run through a few.

00:09:36.100 --> 00:09:39.059
One is a Rhodie, War Machine, from Armor Wars.

00:09:39.059 --> 00:09:40.059
Oh, yeah.

00:09:40.059 --> 00:09:41.059
Oof.

00:09:41.059 --> 00:09:42.059
Rough.

00:09:42.059 --> 00:09:43.059
Bummer.

00:09:43.059 --> 00:09:44.059
Right?

00:09:44.059 --> 00:09:45.059
Right?

00:09:45.059 --> 00:09:46.059
He's been around since Iron Man One.

00:09:46.059 --> 00:09:47.059
Two, Cheadle.

00:09:47.059 --> 00:09:48.059
He's like the old guard, yeah.

00:09:48.059 --> 00:09:52.819
The character has been around since the very
beginning, so it strikes me as a fitting end

00:09:52.819 --> 00:09:56.629
to Armor Wars if he goes out in a blaze of
glory, especially since we're going to have

00:09:56.629 --> 00:10:01.519
Iron Heart coming through in the Black Panther
sequel soon.

00:10:01.519 --> 00:10:03.820
So I see that as a potential exit.

00:10:03.820 --> 00:10:07.619
And again, he's been doing this for a while,
and each project that they do, they command

00:10:07.619 --> 00:10:12.509
a higher and higher paycheck, so eventually,
they may just be like, "Yeah, Don Cheadle,

00:10:12.509 --> 00:10:13.730
we're done.

00:10:13.730 --> 00:10:16.309
You can go do some other prestige television."

00:10:16.309 --> 00:10:18.649
Same deal with Nick Fury.

00:10:18.649 --> 00:10:20.899
Nick fury has been around since the beginning.

00:10:20.899 --> 00:10:24.440
Samuel L. Jackson is getting older.

00:10:24.440 --> 00:10:26.600
How much longer does he want to do this?

00:10:26.600 --> 00:10:30.509
I thought about him, and then I was also like,
"I feel like he just wants to do this forever."

00:10:30.509 --> 00:10:32.339
No, there's that.

00:10:32.339 --> 00:10:33.339
Yeah.

00:10:33.339 --> 00:10:35.319
I mean, again, they're not putting him in
major prosthetics.

00:10:35.319 --> 00:10:38.899
No, he just gets to show up with an eye patch
and be cool every now and then.

00:10:38.899 --> 00:10:40.449
Like, it's not ... yeah.

00:10:40.449 --> 00:10:41.449
Yeah.

00:10:41.449 --> 00:10:44.259
Yeah, so he's doing fine.

00:10:44.259 --> 00:10:46.279
Another one I thought of was Drax the Destroyer.

00:10:46.279 --> 00:10:47.279
Ooh.

00:10:47.279 --> 00:10:49.260
You think they're going to kill Drax?

00:10:49.260 --> 00:10:53.199
I think they could because Guardians of the
Galaxy 3 is going to be in phase four.

00:10:53.199 --> 00:11:00.079
We know that Dave Bautista is not super thrilled
with the Disney machine, right?

00:11:00.079 --> 00:11:04.129
Recently, at the time of this recording, someone
asked him on Twitter like, "Hey, why didn't

00:11:04.129 --> 00:11:06.800
you do the voice of Drax on the second episode
of What If...?"

00:11:06.800 --> 00:11:09.120
He was just like, "How about because they
didn't ask me."

00:11:09.120 --> 00:11:14.500
And it caused this mini-controversy, where
everyone's just like, "We did ask you.

00:11:14.500 --> 00:11:15.500
We asked your agent."

00:11:15.500 --> 00:11:16.899
And then, the agents were like, "You never
asked us."

00:11:16.899 --> 00:11:17.899
I don't know, it's a little-

00:11:17.899 --> 00:11:20.949
He's also getting way more popular.

00:11:20.949 --> 00:11:25.319
Everyone's casting him in everything, I would
say, largely thanks to Guardians.

00:11:25.319 --> 00:11:29.290
He's having his John Cena phase of his career.

00:11:29.290 --> 00:11:30.290
For sure.

00:11:30.290 --> 00:11:34.019
And I would bet that the nature of his contract
was probably not super good because when he

00:11:34.019 --> 00:11:39.360
first signed it, the first Guardians of the
Galaxy was his first major role out of being

00:11:39.360 --> 00:11:40.360
a wrestler.

00:11:40.360 --> 00:11:41.360
Yeah.

00:11:41.360 --> 00:11:43.709
And now, he's a Knives Out 2, a huge leap.

00:11:43.709 --> 00:11:44.709
Yeah.

00:11:44.709 --> 00:11:46.269
So he's probably ready to be done.

00:11:46.269 --> 00:11:48.369
I'm not in the cast of Knives Out 2, somehow.

00:11:48.369 --> 00:11:49.369
None of us are.

00:11:49.369 --> 00:11:50.709
You don't know that.

00:11:50.709 --> 00:11:51.709
That's true.

00:11:51.709 --> 00:11:52.709
I'm actually in the cast of Knives Out 2,
sorry.

00:11:52.709 --> 00:11:53.910
I meant to tell you that.

00:11:53.910 --> 00:11:56.050
I was going to save that for after.

00:11:56.050 --> 00:11:59.879
Please put that in Brian's name tag, "Appearing
in Knives Out 2."

00:11:59.879 --> 00:12:02.220
"Appearing in Knives Out 2."

00:12:02.220 --> 00:12:03.759
So that's so that's one thought.

00:12:03.759 --> 00:12:09.730
So I think a big way to end Guardians of the
Galaxy 3, a big death, right?

00:12:09.730 --> 00:12:11.839
We had Yondu at the end of the second one.

00:12:11.839 --> 00:12:15.480
I don't think that they're going to kill off
Chris Pratt's character.

00:12:15.480 --> 00:12:19.110
They're already working on ... Gomorrah's
already been brought back to life, so it doesn't

00:12:19.110 --> 00:12:21.910
make sense that either of that couple would
get killed off.

00:12:21.910 --> 00:12:25.850
But I do think that Drax feels like he has
a bit of a target on him, especially because

00:12:25.850 --> 00:12:28.800
he's also gone on record as saying he doesn't
like all the makeup application.

00:12:28.800 --> 00:12:30.100
I think he's done with it.

00:12:30.100 --> 00:12:31.139
I think he's done.

00:12:31.139 --> 00:12:35.540
So that's my prediction, but that's actually
not the character I was going to talk about,

00:12:35.540 --> 00:12:40.569
which is Jane Foster in Thor: Love and Thunder.

00:12:40.569 --> 00:12:41.569
Oh.

00:12:41.569 --> 00:12:47.829
I think they brought Natalie Portman back
to do this one movie, where she gets to be

00:12:47.829 --> 00:12:49.230
the protagonist.

00:12:49.230 --> 00:12:54.130
It's going to be the reunion of Jane Foster
and Thor Odinson.

00:12:54.130 --> 00:12:55.189
They're going to reunite.

00:12:55.189 --> 00:12:56.459
That's the love.

00:12:56.459 --> 00:13:00.779
But we also know that from the comics, she
became Thor while she was also undergoing

00:13:00.779 --> 00:13:05.739
treatment for cancer, and that was tied in
with her power, where she was getting chemotherapy,

00:13:05.739 --> 00:13:10.630
but every time she turned into Thor, it would
purge her body of toxins, and so the chemotherapy

00:13:10.630 --> 00:13:11.889
didn't work.

00:13:11.889 --> 00:13:13.899
A common medical ailment.

00:13:13.899 --> 00:13:14.899
Yeah.

00:13:14.899 --> 00:13:17.019
Right, it happens to the best of us.

00:13:17.019 --> 00:13:18.019
It does.

00:13:18.019 --> 00:13:19.339
So at the end of that comic storyline, she
dies.

00:13:19.339 --> 00:13:21.809
Now, because this is comics, she's brought
back to life.

00:13:21.809 --> 00:13:24.699
She gets chemotherapy and she's okay, but
she doesn't have powers anymore.

00:13:24.699 --> 00:13:28.269
But I think this is a Taika Waititi movie.

00:13:28.269 --> 00:13:33.730
This is a guy who's really good at blending
super-duper dramatic, emotional stuff with

00:13:33.730 --> 00:13:34.889
wacky goofy stuff.

00:13:34.889 --> 00:13:40.009
Like, if anyone remembers Scarlett Johannson's
shoes in Jojo Rabbit?

00:13:40.009 --> 00:13:41.470
I was just going to bring that up.

00:13:41.470 --> 00:13:42.910
Oh, that was.

00:13:42.910 --> 00:13:47.709
Mm-hmm. Hunt for the Wilderpeople, that's
some heavy duty stuff in a really fun, funny

00:13:47.709 --> 00:13:48.709
movie.

00:13:48.709 --> 00:13:50.639
But, it's serious stuff.

00:13:50.639 --> 00:13:56.619
Even Thor: Ragnarok has some pretty emotional
stuff where Odin dies.

00:13:56.619 --> 00:14:00.819
It's not necessarily the big cry moment.

00:14:00.819 --> 00:14:02.160
It's much more subdued in that one.

00:14:02.160 --> 00:14:04.029
It's much more of a fun comedy, that movie.

00:14:04.029 --> 00:14:08.569
But I think Taika Waititi, now that he's confident,
now that they're just trusting him to do whatever

00:14:08.569 --> 00:14:09.569
he wants.

00:14:09.569 --> 00:14:11.610
They brought Natalie Portman back.

00:14:11.610 --> 00:14:12.610
They convinced her.

00:14:12.610 --> 00:14:14.529
I think they said, "Hey, do this one movie.

00:14:14.529 --> 00:14:16.239
You're the star of the movie.

00:14:16.239 --> 00:14:22.519
You're going to have a really dramatic death,
and everyone will cry after they saw you kick

00:14:22.519 --> 00:14:28.589
a bunch of ass in the movie, fighting like
Thor, fighting as Thor, and then, at the end,

00:14:28.589 --> 00:14:32.259
you get to die in this tragic dramatic way."

00:14:32.259 --> 00:14:37.860
Man, what a legendary way to go out after
leaving a franchise you weren't really that

00:14:37.860 --> 00:14:40.040
into for the first two movies.

00:14:40.040 --> 00:14:41.040
That's my pick.

00:14:41.040 --> 00:14:42.040
What do you guys think?

00:14:42.040 --> 00:14:43.040
I've been talking a lot.

00:14:43.040 --> 00:14:47.199
That's really good because that would be the
perfect way to get a movie star like Natalie

00:14:47.199 --> 00:14:49.540
Portman to come back to a franchise.

00:14:49.540 --> 00:14:52.509
She famously hated to be like, "It's just
the one movie."

00:14:52.509 --> 00:14:55.850
Because the whole time, I was like, "Oh, she's
coming back because it's Taika Waititi, and

00:14:55.850 --> 00:14:58.309
he has an Oscar, and everyone loves him."

00:14:58.309 --> 00:15:01.079
I mean, I'm guessing people are lining up
to work with him.

00:15:01.079 --> 00:15:04.329
I would, if I were an actor.

00:15:04.329 --> 00:15:06.069
I just want to work with him now.

00:15:06.069 --> 00:15:09.600
I just want to hang out while he writes and
be like, "What are you doing?

00:15:09.600 --> 00:15:10.629
What are you doing?

00:15:10.629 --> 00:15:11.629
What are you writing?"

00:15:11.629 --> 00:15:12.629
"What is it now?

00:15:12.629 --> 00:15:13.629
What scene is it this time?"

00:15:13.629 --> 00:15:15.869
You'll get the call after Knives Out 2 comes
out.

00:15:15.869 --> 00:15:21.379
No, but that's a good point, that maybe they
were like, "Hey, you only have to do one thing.

00:15:21.379 --> 00:15:23.619
We're not going to pin you too."

00:15:23.619 --> 00:15:27.769
Because, I mean, it has to be one thing or
the other with her, right?

00:15:27.769 --> 00:15:33.199
Either she dies, or she takes up the mantle
from Chris Hemsworth, I would think.

00:15:33.199 --> 00:15:37.019
I mean, that's entirely possible too because
Chris Hemsworth's been doing this for a while.

00:15:37.019 --> 00:15:42.559
But from what I understand in my limited role
as guy on the internet, he seems to really

00:15:42.559 --> 00:15:43.939
love doing Thor.

00:15:43.939 --> 00:15:45.699
Is that who you're playing in Knives Out 2?

00:15:45.699 --> 00:15:46.699
Yeah.

00:15:46.699 --> 00:15:48.910
I'm playing "guy on the internet" in Knives
Out 2.

00:15:48.910 --> 00:15:50.639
I'm just doing this.

00:15:50.639 --> 00:15:51.899
I'm just typing on my keyboard.

00:15:51.899 --> 00:15:53.290
Don't spoil it for us, God.

00:15:53.290 --> 00:15:59.559
I don't want to know anything.

00:15:59.559 --> 00:16:01.749
But yeah, I think Chris Hemsworth really likes
doing this.

00:16:01.749 --> 00:16:05.610
And so, I think having Natalie Portman come
in, it doesn't make sense that she's going

00:16:05.610 --> 00:16:07.319
